theorem algebra-at-a-member
  note        A step said of every member is read at a member by algebra,
              as by membership: i + i = 2·i at i.
  let n ∈ ℕ    (H1)
  then For all i ∈ {1, …, n}, i + i = 2·i.

1.  For all i ∈ {1, …, n}, i + i = 2·i.
    algebra

theorem inequalities-at-a-member
  note        And by inequalities, which takes what the member's membership
              implies, i ≥ 1 of i ∈ ℕ.
  then For all i ∈ ℕ, i + 1 > 1.

1.  For all i ∈ ℕ, i + 1 > 1.
    inequalities
